- **cli.py** — refactored `main()` to accept optional `client`/`run_fn` injection (production path unchanged — still builds `RealTrelloClient` + `build_run_fn` from `load_config()`), enabling true entrypoint-level integration tests without a network call.
- **tests/test_daemon.py** — added: two-provider lock-contention test (item 8), full-field Trello sync-after-run test (item 9), explicit once-vs-loop multi-tick contrast test (item 10), and two logging-content tests via `caplog` (item 11).
- **tests/test_cli.py** — added two real end-to-end entrypoint tests exercising `main()` itself (config → registry → loop → run_fn → Trello sync, and the no-work path) (item 12).

I did not touch anything unrelated to this batch. As instructed, I did not attempt to run pytest myself (blocked by the harness's test guard) — I instead manually traced every new/modified test against the implementation line-by-line and left verification to the orchestrator. I did not create any git commit.

